-- Q3540: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Automatic failover to surviving nodes, minimizing service downtime","Faster internet connectivity and reduced network latency for users","Improved physical security controls within the data center facility","Encryption of data stored on disk to prevent unauthorized access"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1 Section 5.1.1, server clustering groups multiple servers as a single logical unit, providing automatic failover when one node fails. Surviving nodes absorb the failed node''s workload, minimizing or eliminating downtime.
Wrong (B): Clustering addresses server-level redundancy, not internet speed or network latency optimization.
Wrong (C): Physical security involves facility access controls and environmental protections, unrelated to server clustering.
Wrong (D): Disk encryption protects data confidentiality at rest but does not provide availability or failover capability.$EXPL$
