-- Q3548: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Tripling the processing capacity of a single server beyond normal load","Complete protection against all possible simultaneous failure scenarios","Backup capability covering only half of the active server components","One additional component beyond minimum required for single-failure protection"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per the Uptime Institute Tier Classification and NIST SP 800-34, N+1 redundancy means operating one more component than the minimum (N) required for normal operations. This provides automatic failover protection against any single component failure at reasonable cost.
Wrong (A): Tripling capacity describes scaling up a single server, not adding a redundant standby component.
Wrong (B): N+1 protects against single-component failures only, not all simultaneous failure scenarios (that would require higher redundancy like 2N).
Wrong (C): Covering only half the active components would leave significant gaps and does not match any standard redundancy model.$EXPL$
