-- Q3568: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["No risk, because maintaining the CMDB is optional for IT operations","They are invisible to patching, change impact, and disaster recovery processes","Undocumented servers perform better because they avoid management overhead","The CMDB will automatically discover and register all missing server assets"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per ITIL 4 configuration management and COBIT 2019 BAI10, servers absent from the CMDB are invisible to IT management. They may be missed during security patching, excluded from change impact assessments, and overlooked in disaster recovery planning, creating significant unmanaged risk.
