-- Q3569: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["A fully operational facility with current data, ready for immediate failover","A facility with pre-installed hardware and connectivity but no current data loaded","A facility providing only space, power, and environmental controls requiring full setup","A mobile trailer equipped with satellite connectivity and portable equipment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1, a cold site is the most basic and least expensive DR facility, providing only physical space, power, cooling, and basic connectivity. All hardware, software, and data must be installed and restored before operations resume, resulting in days-to-weeks recovery time.
Wrong (A): This describes a hot site with real-time data replication and near-immediate failover capability, the most expensive option.
Wrong (B): This describes a warm site, which has hardware pre-installed but lacks current data, offering a middle ground between hot and cold sites.
Wrong (D): A mobile site is a separate DR category and does not match the definition of a cold site.$EXPL$
