-- Q3570: System Availability and Change Management [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Every dependency is a potential failure point and must be included in recovery plans","Only the primary application requires disaster recovery protection and planning","Dependent systems should be consolidated into one application to reduce complexity","Interdependent systems have no meaningful effect on overall process recovery time"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1, interdependency analysis reveals that each system a business process depends on is a potential single point of failure. The slowest system to recover determines actual process recovery time, so all dependencies must be addressed in DR planning.
Wrong (B): Ignoring upstream and downstream dependencies creates blind spots where a recovered primary application cannot function without its dependent systems.
Wrong (C): Consolidating systems may introduce new risks and is an architectural decision, not a BCP finding about recovery sequencing.
Wrong (D): Dependencies directly affect recovery time because a process cannot function until all required systems are operational.$EXPL$
