  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Clause 6.1.3(d), the Statement of Applicability is a required document listing all 93 Annex A controls, stating whether each is applicable, and justifying inclusions and exclusions based on the risk assessment. It bridges risk findings to control selection for certification.
Wrong (A): An access control matrix documents user permissions, not the applicability of framework controls.
Wrong (B): An incident log records security events; the SoA addresses control applicability, not historical incidents.
Wrong (D): Budget documentation is a financial planning activity unrelated to the ISO 27001 certification requirement for control applicability.$EXPL$
