-- Q3594: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Controls may be implemented but certification requires a formal accredited audit","Self-declaration is sufficient to claim full ISO 27001 certification status","ISO 27001 does not require any form of third-party audit or assessment","The client should switch to NIST CSF, which has no certification requirement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Clauses 9.2 and 9.3, formal certification requires assessment by an accredited third-party certification body. An organization can implement controls and self-declare alignment, but only independent external audit constitutes formal certification.
Wrong (B): Self-declaration demonstrates intent and internal conformance but does not satisfy the external audit requirement for certification.
Wrong (C): ISO 27001 explicitly requires both internal audits and, for certification, third-party assessment by an accredited body.
Wrong (D): Switching frameworks does not resolve the issue; the client''s claim of ISO 27001 certification specifically requires accredited audit.$EXPL$
