-- Q3599: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Monitoring must track both deficiency detection and remediation completion to confirm controls function over time","MTTD is not a recognized metric under any framework, requiring the entire monitoring program to be rebuilt","COSO does not address IT security controls because it applies only to financial reporting within accounting","Monitoring Activities only requires annual review by external auditors, not ongoing internal metric tracking"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per COSO Internal Control Integrated Framework (2013), Principle 16, Monitoring Activities requires tracking both detection of deficiencies and timely remediation to evaluate whether controls are present and functioning over time. MTTD alone measures detection speed without confirming identified problems are resolved.
Wrong (B): MTTD is a widely recognized security operations metric used across multiple frameworks; the issue is its incompleteness, not its validity.
Wrong (C): COSO applies to all organizational controls including IT security, not only financial reporting within accounting departments.
Wrong (D): Monitoring Activities requires ongoing monitoring built into daily operations, not merely annual external auditor review.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3599;

-- Q3600: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both belong under Technological controls because they involve identity verification through IT systems","Both belong under People controls because they address personnel screening and individual access governance","Background check is Physical and visitor badge is Organizational because they involve different departments","Both belong under Organizational controls because all governance activities default to that theme"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ISO 27002:2022 Sections 5-8, the People controls theme covers human-related safeguards. Employee background checks (personnel screening) and visitor badge policies (governing physical access by individuals) both address people-centric security measures distinct from Organizational, Physical, and Technological themes.
Wrong (A): Technological controls address IT system safeguards like encryption and access control software, not personnel-focused activities.
Wrong (C): Neither control fits these categories; both are people-centric measures classified under the People theme in ISO 27002:2022.
Wrong (D): Organizational controls cover policies, roles, and responsibilities at the governance level, not specific personnel screening or visitor management activities.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3600;

