-- Q3603: Security and Control Frameworks [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Asset inventories are foundational because you cannot protect unknown assets","Regulatory agencies mandate that these specific controls be implemented first","Asset and software inventories generate the most audit evidence of all controls","They are listed first because they are the easiest controls to implement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per CIS Controls v8, aligned with NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 (CM-8), Controls 1 and 2 are listed first because they are foundational to every other security activity. Without knowing what hardware and software exists, organizations cannot effectively apply patches, manage configurations, or monitor for threats.
Wrong (B): CIS numbering reflects logical dependency, not regulatory mandate. No regulation requires these controls be implemented in this specific order.
Wrong (C): While inventories support audit activities, they are prioritized for their foundational role in enabling all downstream security controls, not for evidence generation.
Wrong (D): Ease of implementation does not determine CIS ordering; asset inventories can be complex to implement thoroughly across large organizations.$EXPL$
